senses.gloss:
(I) (गण)--born of साध्या and Dharma: their son was Arthasiddhi;
1: भा. VI. 6. 7; Br. II. २४. २७; ३८. 3.
created by वामदेव; of the तामस epoch;
2: M. 4. ३०; 5. १७; 9. १६.
one of the 7 गणस् of the Vaivasvata epoch.
3: Ib. 9. २९; वा. १०. ७१; २१. २२; ३०. ९९.

(II)--the twelve sons of Dharma and साध्या; superior to Gods; first created as जयादेवस् from the face of ब्रह्मा, again born in स्वायम्भुव epoch as Jitas, in तामस epoch as Harayas, in Raivata epoch as वैकुण्ठस्, स्वारोचिष epoch as तुषितस्, in Uttama epoch as Satyas, in चाक्षुष epoch as छान्दजस्, and in the Vaivasvata epoch as साध्यस्; Vasus are their brothers; Gods of चाक्षुष and Vaivasvata epochs; their names are Mana, Anumanta, प्राण, Nara, अपान, वीर्यवान्, वीति, Naya, Haya, Hamsa, नारायण, Vibhu, and Prabhu; live in Bhuvarloka; नारा- यण, their overlord;
1: Br. III. 3. 4-२०, ५८, ६७; 4. ३३. 8 6; १०. ८८; IV. 2. २८; १५. २४, २०. ४६; ३०. 8.; M. ३६. 1; १३२. 3; १७१. ४२; २०३. १०-12; २४६. ५४; २४७. १०; वा. ६६. 4-१२; १०१. ३०; Vi. I. 9. ६४ and ७०.
worship gau, the mind-born daughter of the मानस manes;
2: M. १५. १५.
requested Soma to give up जारा to बृहस्पति;
3: Ib. २३. ३५.
with Angirasa's sons spread themselves in the world of Marici Garbha.
4: वा. ७३. ३८.

5: Ib. V. 1. १७.
